# Content Authoring Guidelines

## Frontmatter Schema

Every content file must have valid frontmatter:

```yaml
---
title: "Your Title Here"
date: 2026-01-15          # ISO 8601, required
description: "One sentence summary for SEO and listing pages"
tags: [tag1, tag2]        # optional
draft: false              # true = excluded from build
---
```

## Blog Posts (`src/content/blog/`)
- Short, focused entries (300–1500 words)
- Filename = URL slug: `2026-01-15-my-post.md`
- Conversational but professional tone
- Polish or English (indicate language in frontmatter if needed)

## Articles (`src/content/articles/`)
- Long-form, technical or professional content (1500+ words)
- Filename = URL slug: `topic-name.md`
- Include subheadings (`##`, `###`) for navigation
- Code blocks with language identifier: ` ```typescript `

## Markdown Conventions
- H1 is the title (from frontmatter) — do NOT add an `# H1` in body
- Use `##` and `###` for sections within content
- Prefer reference links for external URLs at the bottom of the file
- Images: `![alt text](../../assets/image.jpg)` — place images in `src/assets/`
